From f2d55a104350065b4460854a754bbaaf71962f32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:36:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: let the user choose which hour the scheduled check
 runs in

Owner asked for a box, appearing when Scheduled Check is enabled, to set the
check time - assuming it was cron. It is not: the check is
auto_firmware_check_reaper() (our rename of Merlin's auto_firmware_check_merlin)
driven from the watchdog loop, firing when

    local.tm_hour == (2 + rand_hr) && local.tm_min == rand_min

with rand_hr = rand%4 and rand_min = rand%60 both drawn ONCE AT BOOT. So it has
always run at a random time between 02:00 and 05:59, moving on every reboot,
with nothing user-visible and no nvram behind it. There was no time to expose -
it had to be built.

  firmware_check_hour   new nvram. Empty = automatic, which is exactly the
                        behaviour above. 0-23 pins the hour.

THE MINUTE STAYS RANDOM EITHER WAY, and that is deliberate rather than an
omission. This check pulls a GitHub-hosted manifest, so an exact user-visible
time would let a whole fleet name the same minute and arrive together; the
default would concentrate hardest of all. Pinning the hour is what the request
actually wants - "check overnight, not in the middle of the day" - while the
minute inside it is noise to the user and load-spreading to us. An out-of-range
or junk value falls back to automatic rather than failing closed, so a bad nvram
value can never stop the check running.

UI: the picker is revealed by the same toggle that owns the feature and rides
the same save, so there is no second Apply and no state where a time is set but
the check is off. A stale value that no longer matches an option resets the
select to Automatic instead of showing blank.

RFWU_45..47 minted and English-seeded across 25 packs, lockstep 6635 -> 6638.
RFWU_46 renders inside a JS backtick template; all three values are free of
quotes, apostrophes and backticks (rule 29 checked across every pack).

NOT COMPILE-VERIFIED: watchdog.c cannot be built standalone - the router package
makefiles need the parent env - so the C rides the next full build. atoi and
nvram_get are both long-established in this file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
